  {
    "id": "song-burn-this",
    "title": "Burn This",
    "type": "Original",
    "status": "Live Ready",
    "key": "Em",
    "capo": "None",
    "bpm": "118",
    "timeSig": "4/4",
    "timeSignature": "4/4",
    "writers": "Matthew Brandabur (©2009)",
    "coWriters": "Matthew Brandabur (©2009)",
    "tags": [
      "Indie Rock",
      "Driving",
      "Acoustic",
      "Set Opener"
    ],
    "chords": "Em, D (Chorus: F#m, G#, Bm7, DMaj7, C, F)",
    "quickChords": "Em, D (Chorus: F#m, G#, Bm7, DMaj7, C, F)",
    "notes": "Stage submix: Guitar into Notepad-5 Channel 1 with Hi-Z engaged, Master XLR L/R to FOH.",
    "lyrics": "[INTRO]\n| Em        | D         | Em        | D         |\n\n[VERSE 1]\nEm                                          D\nBurn this \"I love you,\" don't let nobody see\nEm                                          D\nBurn this \"I need you,\" don't you be afraid of me\nEm                          D\nBurn this with your clothes on\nEm                          D\nForget me with your shades drawn\nEm                                          D\nI wrote this \"I love you,\" it was so not my style\nEm                                          D\nBurn this \"I need you,\" can you walk for a while?\nEm                                          D\nYou slowed down this morning to give me one more warning\n< KICKS >\n\n[PRE-CHORUS 1]\n< KICKS >\n        Cmaj7\nYou don't remember...\n                                   B7\nYou said: \"Tell me you know it's me\"\n\n[CHORUS]\nF#m          G#          Bm7           DMaj7\nFires that left us bleeding\n                         (a reason to not stop weeping)\nFires that showed us screaming\n               C                    F\nDon't you need one, kitten, a fire of your own?\n\n[VERSE 2]\nEm                                  D\nAugust, I thought I used to be so alive\nEm                                  D\nSeptember, I'm sorry, can you wait till we've died?\nEm                          D\nForgetting that I can't see you\nEm                          D\nBeing my pet don't please you\nEm                          D\nGo back to the one that needs you\n< KICKS >\nWe saw skies of red — scrapers dead\n\n[PRE-CHORUS 2]\n        Cmaj7\nDon't you remember...\n                                   B7\nYou said: \"Tell me you know it's me\"\n        Cmaj7\nThe war was waiting...\n                                   B7\nYou said: \"Tell me you know it's me\"\n        Am\nThe sun was shining...\n                                   G\nYou said: \"Tell me you know it's me\"\n\n[CHORUS]\nF#m          G#          Bm7           DMaj7\nFires that left us bleeding\n                         (a reason to not stop weeping)\nFires that showed us screaming\n               C\nDon't we need one, kitten, need one, need one...\n          F\nA fire of our own?\n\n[VERSE 3]\nEm                                         D\nBurn this, I think you said it's all for the best\nEm                                         D\nBurn this, I knew there would be nothing left\nEm                          D\nWalls fall down like laughter\nEm                          D\nAnd you know what comes after\n          Cmaj7\nYour plane was leaving...\n                                   B7\nYou made me whisper: \"You know it's me\"\n\n[OUTRO]\n| Em        | D         | Em        | D         |\nFinal Hit: Em (Ring out)",
    "updatedAt": "2026-11-15T17:38:00.000Z",
    "updatedAtFormatted": "Nov 15, 2026, 9:38 AM",
    "lastSaved": "2026-11-15T17:38:00.000Z",
    "audios": [],
    "memos": []
  },
